# [OAUTH](../wg/oauth.html)

## Summary

This document records the minutes for the OAUTH Working Group virtual interim meeting (Interim 2026-OAUTH-10). The session focused on AI agent authorization and featured a deep-dive presentation on "mission-bound authorization"—a framework to govern approved work rather than relying solely on credentials and access tokens. 

Karl McGuinness presented the framework, detailing how agent intent can be shaped into deterministic, user-approved authority ("missions"), how missions bind to OAuth tokens, mechanisms for job-level revocation, and a proposed Minimum Viable Product (MVP). The working group discussed the scope of protocol changes, handling dynamic authority discovery, resource server requirements, and how to manage the complexity of overlapping agent authorization proposals.

